WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.250
- Good morning. I'm walking
to the train right now.

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:06.453
We're going to the airport today. Yay!

00:00:08.129 --> 00:00:13.040
(upbeat music)

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.883
- [Voiceover] We're currently in the car

00:00:23.883 --> 00:00:26.016
on the way to San Fransisco.

00:00:26.016 --> 00:00:30.776
I am playing this really
basic app about Swift

00:00:30.776 --> 00:00:33.767
before the conference so
I'm not wasting car time.

00:00:34.143 --> 00:00:36.883
- We're stuck on the airport
for like seven hours,

00:00:36.883 --> 00:00:38.921
so I thought I'd get some work done.

00:00:39.274 --> 00:00:42.740
This is my new app. We
wanna launch it this week.

00:00:43.222 --> 00:00:45.585
Excited to get some of it done.

00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:51.441
- [Voiceover] Growing up I
actually did not have any idea

00:00:51.441 --> 00:00:53.183
that I was gonna end up

00:00:53.183 --> 00:00:55.569
being a developer or a designer.

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:57.594
- I never thought that
I could actually code

00:00:57.594 --> 00:00:59.586
and make proper apps.

00:01:01.586 --> 00:01:04.020
Because it was somebody else's thing.

00:01:04.421 --> 00:01:07.160
- Wild Ski is a skiing app that we made.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:10.434
It's a game where animals
come from the jungle

00:01:10.434 --> 00:01:11.868
and go to the mountain.

00:01:12.152 --> 00:01:15.984
- My first game that I posted
is called Operation B.R.A.I.N.

00:01:15.984 --> 00:01:18.189
Growing up, I always hated math.

00:01:18.189 --> 00:01:20.418
I think the way that it's presented to us,

00:01:20.418 --> 00:01:23.120
it's like a prison. It's a cage.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:25.452
Apps can change education,
and we need that.

00:01:25.619 --> 00:01:27.988
- I have two apps that
are on the App Store.

00:01:27.988 --> 00:01:31.355
One is a game called Knightly
Moves that's based on chess,

00:01:31.355 --> 00:01:34.884
and then I have another app
called Healthy Food Compass,

00:01:34.884 --> 00:01:38.245
which'll help you find
healthy food on-the-go.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:41.961
- Right now I'm developing
my first solo app.

00:01:41.961 --> 00:01:44.018
It's called President.

00:01:44.018 --> 00:01:46.692
It's going to allow people to

00:01:46.692 --> 00:01:50.255
look at, track, follow,
discover the presidential events

00:01:50.255 --> 00:01:52.478
for the 2016 election.

00:01:55.526 --> 00:01:57.592
- [Voiceover] I don't know who it is.

00:01:57.592 --> 00:01:58.405
- We think ...

00:01:58.405 --> 00:02:00.280
- It's Tim Cook, yeah.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:03.838
- I would tell him that I'm
thankful for his existence.

00:02:03.838 --> 00:02:05.530
- If I met Tim Cook, I would ask him

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:07.060
to take a selfie with me.

00:02:07.112 --> 00:02:09.202
- I think I'd just hope
that I would have something

00:02:09.202 --> 00:02:10.520
to say at all.

00:02:12.005 --> 00:02:17.005
(crowd talking)

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.621
(camera noises)

00:02:39.541 --> 00:02:40.865
(camera noises)

00:02:44.935 --> 00:02:46.945
(camera noises)

00:02:47.765 --> 00:02:50.089
- I'm so glad that I got to say that.

00:02:50.119 --> 00:02:54.019
- Taking a selfie with someone
who changed my life is,

00:02:54.019 --> 00:02:56.179
like I never thought
this was gonna happen.

00:02:56.179 --> 00:02:59.122
I mean, I can't believe it right now.

00:02:59.708 --> 00:03:01.397
(upbeat music)

00:03:01.397 --> 00:03:03.144
- This is it.

00:03:03.144 --> 00:03:04.779
- We feel very official.

00:03:06.405 --> 00:03:07.866
- [Voiceover] What are we doing right now?

00:03:07.866 --> 00:03:08.811
What are we waiting for?

00:03:08.811 --> 00:03:11.907
- We are going to Keynote.

00:03:11.907 --> 00:03:13.876
- Which we're super happy that we ...

00:03:13.876 --> 00:03:14.800
- Got a spot.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:15.683
- Got seats.

00:03:15.683 --> 00:03:18.098
- Because I've been watching it from home

00:03:18.098 --> 00:03:20.280
for the past couple of years,

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:22.179
and I really want to see it live.

00:03:22.532 --> 00:03:25.388
- I'm eager to see how
it's actually gonna be

00:03:25.388 --> 00:03:27.465
and feel the real experience.

00:03:28.013 --> 00:03:33.006
(upbeat music)

00:03:37.555 --> 00:03:39.830
- [Tim Cook] Our youngest
scholarship winner

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:41.799
is a 12 year old girl from New York.

00:03:42.005 --> 00:03:46.997
(applause)

00:03:47.562 --> 00:03:48.956
- [Voiceover] When Tim Cook mentioned me,

00:03:48.956 --> 00:03:51.493
it felt really awesome

00:03:51.493 --> 00:03:53.593
that I just stood out.

00:03:53.593 --> 00:03:54.969
- I've always heard about it.

00:03:54.969 --> 00:03:56.687
Like, "Oh my god, all these people want

00:03:56.687 --> 00:03:58.640
"to go to the Keynote" and all that,

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:01.569
and then to even be able to go there

00:04:01.569 --> 00:04:02.992
was just amazing.

00:04:02.992 --> 00:04:05.653
- I never expected to be here

00:04:05.653 --> 00:04:07.856
at any point in time when I started.

00:04:07.856 --> 00:04:11.524
- I never expected it to
take me places like this.

00:04:11.524 --> 00:04:15.530
- I'm just so excited to
use this new skill set

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:17.579
towards things that I believe.

00:04:17.579 --> 00:04:20.222
- One thing I would say to
a girl who's just starting

00:04:20.222 --> 00:04:24.365
is that don't give up just
because it's dominated by men

00:04:24.365 --> 00:04:27.370
because in the future, it'll hopefully

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.746
be more women in coding.

00:04:30.262 --> 00:04:33.536
- I would tell a girl also
to reach out to people.

00:04:33.536 --> 00:04:36.160
To talk about her app,
get all their feedback

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:40.223
because from one email, we ended up here,

00:04:40.223 --> 00:04:43.056
so not to be afraid to
share with the world

00:04:43.056 --> 00:04:44.635
her app and what it does,

00:04:44.635 --> 00:04:46.673
and then who knows where
that's gonna take her.

00:04:46.864 --> 00:04:50.091
- I'm really looking forward
to continuing on this journey.

00:04:50.091 --> 00:04:53.127
I have no plans on stopping.

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:57.493
(upbeat music)

